cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "agda-groups: finite group theory in Agda"
abstract: >-
  A library of finite group theory in Agda, on the group theory of the Agda
  Universal Algebra Library, whose modules it imports rather than copies.
  A finite group is a group of that library with an irredundant enumeration
  of its carrier, and a subgroup is a decidable subgroup, given by
  generators where it can be, with equality of subgroups as a pair of
  inclusions; this is how a finite group and its subgroups are counted.  On
  that representation the library is to develop cosets and the index,
  Lagrange's theorem, group actions and the orbit-stabilizer theorem, the
  product formula, normalizers, centralizers and the center, conjugacy
  classes and the class equation, quotient groups and the correspondence
  theorem, Cayley's theorem, p-groups and their centers, Cauchy's theorem,
  Sylow's three theorems in full, fixed-point-free automorphisms, abelian
  minimal normal subgroups, perfect groups, and the complements of an
  abelian normal subgroup and their 1-cocycles.  Each result is stated as a
  textbook of finite group theory states it and cites its number there,
  Aschbacher's Finite Group Theory first.  Every module is checked under
  --without-K --exact-split --safe, with no postulate.
authors:
  - family-names: "DeMeo"
    given-names: "William"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1832-5690"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/ualib/agda-groups"
keywords:
  - Agda
  - group theory
  - finite groups
  - Sylow theorems
  - universal algebra
  - constructive mathematics
  - formal verification
